**Considering React Implementation**

I’m thinking we likely need a generic answer about React. I should mention setting the wrapper's position to relative, the input’s padding-right, and positioning the button absolutely to the right. Including an SVG inside the button for the onClick event sounds like a good idea too. Accessibility is important, so I’ll keep that in mind while discussing code. I'll make sure to cover these details clearly!
[/Thinking]

Use a wrapper with `position: relative`, then place the SVG/icon button absolutely on the right side of the input.

Example in React:

```jsx
import { useState } from "react";

function SearchInput() {
  const [value, setValue] = useState("");

  const handleSearch = () => {
    console.log("Searching for:", value);
    // call your function here
  };

  return (
    <div style={{ position: "relative", width: "300px" }}>
      <input
        type="text"
        value={value}
        onChange={(e) => setValue(e.target.value)}
        placeholder="Search..."
        style={{
          width: "100%",
          padding: "10px 40px 10px 12px",
          boxSizing: "border-box",
        }}
      />

      <button
        type="button"
        onClick={handleSearch}
        style={{
          position: "absolute",
          right: "10px",
          top: "50%",
          transform: "translateY(-50%)",
          border: "none",
          background: "transparent",
          cursor: "pointer",
          padding: 0,
          display: "flex",
          alignItems: "center",
        }}
      >
        <svg
          width="20"
          height="20"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          strokeWidth="2"
          strokeLinecap="round"
          strokeLinejoin="round"
        >
          <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8" />
          <line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65" />
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>
  );
}

export default SearchInput;
```

If you want the function to run only when the input has text:

```jsx
const handleSearch = () => {
  if (!value.trim()) return;

  console.log("Searching for:", value);
};
```

The important parts are:

```css
.wrapper {
  position: relative;
}

input {
  padding-right: 40px;
}

button {
  position: absolute;
  right: 10px;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
}
```

